{"resource":{"id":"go-quick-revision-notes","title":"Go — Quick Revision Notes","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"6 min","pages":6,"lastUpdated":"January 2026","tags":["Programming","Go","Concurrency"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Condensed Go revision notes — one-liners, mnemonics, tables, and interview keywords for the night before your exam or interview."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. One-liners"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Mnemonics"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Interview Keywords"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Common Syntax"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Quick Tables"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Cheat Summaries"},{"id":"review","label":"Revision Review"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Go — Cheat Sheet","tag":"Programming","time":"5 min"},{"title":"Go — PDF Notes","tag":"Programming","time":"52 min"},{"title":"Go — Beginner Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"17 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Refresh core Go concepts in under 10 minutes.</li>\n          <li>Memorise interview-critical facts and mnemonics.</li>\n          <li>Have a compact glance-friendly reference the day before an assessment.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. One-liners</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Go is statically typed, compiled, and garbage-collected.</li>\n          <li>Every file starts with <code>package X</code>; <code>main</code> is entry.</li>\n          <li><code>:=</code> is the short variable declaration (function-scope only).</li>\n          <li>Zero values everywhere — no <code>undefined</code>.</li>\n          <li>Interfaces are satisfied implicitly.</li>\n          <li>Errors are values. Wrap with <code>%w</code>.</li>\n          <li><code>go</code> starts a goroutine; <code>chan</code> is the communication primitive.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Mnemonics</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>SCIM</strong> — <em>Slice, Channel, Interface, Map</em>: the four reference-y types.</li>\n          <li><strong>CATS</strong> — always pass <em>Context, Args, Timeouts, State</em> to long ops.</li>\n          <li><strong>SEE</strong> — every goroutine needs a <em>Start, Exit path, Error path</em>.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517694712202-14dd9538aa97?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Rapid-recall card: SCIM, CATS, and SEE cover 80% of interview mistakes.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Interview Keywords</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Goroutine · Channel · Mutex · Context · Deadline · Panic vs error · Interface satisfaction · Embedding · Slice header · Escape analysis · GC pause · <code>go test -race</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Common Syntax</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Task</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Snippet</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Variable</td><td class=\"p-2\"><code>x := 10</code></td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Slice</td><td class=\"p-2\"><code>s := []int{1,2}</code></td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Map</td><td class=\"p-2\"><code>m := map[string]int{}</code></td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Goroutine</td><td class=\"p-2\"><code>go f()</code></td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Channel</td><td class=\"p-2\"><code>c := make(chan int)</code></td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Quick Tables</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Slice vs Array</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Choose</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Dynamic size</td><td class=\"p-2\">Slice</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Fixed known size</td><td class=\"p-2\">Array</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Channel workflow at a glance: producer → buffered channel → consumers.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Cheat Summaries</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Concurrency:</strong> share by communicating, not by sharing memory.</li>\n          <li><strong>Errors:</strong> return them, wrap them, log them once at the boundary.</li>\n          <li><strong>APIs:</strong> accept interfaces, return structs.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"review\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Revision Review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Top Concepts</h3>\n        <p>Goroutines, channels, interfaces, error wrapping, context propagation.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Rapid Recall</h3>\n        <p>Slice header (ptr, len, cap) · Map is unordered · Nil channel blocks forever.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Interview Checklist</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Can you explain the memory model?</li>\n          <li>Can you spot a race condition in a code snippet?</li>\n          <li>Can you design a bounded worker pool?</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is this enough for an interview?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Combine with the PDF Notes — this is refresh, not learn-from-scratch.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need to memorise everything?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Only the tables and mnemonics.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Escape analysis</strong> — the compiler deciding heap vs stack allocation.</li>\n          <li><strong>Deadlock</strong> — two goroutines waiting on each other forever.</li>\n          <li><strong>Panic</strong> — an unrecoverable error; use only for truly exceptional cases.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          Condensed for revision — do not rely on this alone for exam preparation. Refer to official\n          documentation and the full PDF Notes for depth. Trademarks belong to their respective owners.\n        </p>\n      </div></section>"}